{
  "q0": "The group decided to keep the curve but would remove either the yellow color or rubber material to stay within the 12.5 Euro budget. They decided against removing the curve because it would make the remote 'far more ordinary' and they wanted to 'separate it from the rest of the remote control world'.",
  "q1": "The group chose 'Triple R_' as the product name after discussing alternatives like 'banana remote', 'R_C_ deluxe', and 'Real Reactor', selecting it for being short, catchy, and aligned with the company's 'Real Reaction' brand.",
  "q2": "The group discussed reducing costs from 17 Euros to 12.5 Euros by removing speech recognition (the most expensive feature) and the special yellow color (replaced with black and grey), while keeping the curve and rubber material to meet budget constraints.",
  "q3": "'Triple R' was preferred over 'triple RC' because it doesn't look like 'triple remote control' and is more concise, as the Project Manager explained that 'the first one looks like it's a triple remote control, but it's only a single remote control'."
}

{
  "q0": "Industrial Designer rejected solar energy because it 'may not be so good when you're watching TV in the night'",
  "q1": "Industrial Designer thought speech recognition was 'a great idea' but was 'not convinced we can put it into this box for the price that we need'",
  "q2": "According to Marketing, the revolution of interaction was necessary because 'the current styles are just plain awful' and they 'definitely wanna be inspired'",
  "q3": "The discussion focused on functions (power, channel, volume, enter key, number keys, big user-friendly buttons) and power sources (rechargeable batteries vs. A_A_ batteries vs. solar), with Industrial Designer rejecting solar due to nighttime TV use issues"
